s in development is a joint project of the Commission on History and the Social Sciences (CHASS) and the Committee on Development Studies (CODES) of the Council on Foreign Relations for the purpose of providing a nationally and internationally accessible catalog of resources on the history of truth, lies, and misperceptions about development.

The site has a wide range of resources, including:

articles on falsehoods and their evolution;

views on the history of falsehoods;

a list of "leading" falsehoods (false claims which are repeated in a variety of contexts);

an annotated bibliography;

a list of resources in the public domain;

a list of secondary resources; and

a series of "commentary and rebuttal" essays.

